# Sacrifice a dwarf corpse at an altar of Khasrach, the orc god.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sacrifice-wildcard.keys 1
#
# This is the oracle for inc-upw.27. Khasrach's SACRIFICE_LIST
# (lib/religion.irh:2828) is seven rows: MA_ORC, MA_GOBLINOID, then five
# MA_ALL rows. MA_ALL is 0, and Character::Sacrifice used to stop the list at
# the first zero in the left slot, so the five MA_ALL rows were unreachable
# and a dwarf -- neither orc nor goblinoid -- matched nothing.
#
#   before the fix:  "Khasrach seems uninterested in your offering."
#   after the fix:   "Khasrach is impressed" and, because wizard mode is on,
#                    "(sacVal 88, gained 88, favour 88, ...)"
#
# Run with tools/check_sacrifice.sh, which asserts both of those.
#
# WHY THIS SCRIPT IS SEED-LOCKED. It only works at seed 1, and every step
# below depends on that:
#  * chargen.keys makes a male orc barbarian, and at this seed the game hands
#    him Khasrach -- the character sheet shows a "Holy symbol of Khasrach".
#    The fix is about Khasrach's list specifically, so a different patron
#    measures nothing.
#  * The Goblin Caves entry chamber at this seed is littered with corpses.
#    END then LEFT*5 walks onto a dwarf corpse. There is no way to ask the
#    game "walk to the nearest dwarf corpse", so the moves are counted.
#  * [w] is the dwarf corpse's letter in the "Offer what?" menu. Menu letters
#    move when the item list changes, exactly as chargen.keys warns.
# If any of that drifts, the run will fail loudly on the asserted text rather
# than quietly measure the wrong thing.
#
# The altar is made by wizard option [M] "Create Altar" (src/Debug.cpp),
# which exists for this: a sacrifice needs the player to be standing on an
# altar, and the only other source of one is MakeLev's random placement
# (src/MakeLev.cpp:2107-2123), which cannot be asked for a particular god.

@include chargen.keys

END                 # step south-west, off the arrival square
LEFT*5              # ...and west onto the dwarf corpse

w                   # wizard mode -- lowercase, see the SHIFT note in
y                   # Wposix.cpp TokenToKey; 'W' is a different keystroke
M                   # [M] Create Altar
"Khasrach"
ENTER

p                   # pray; patron and altar agree, so the prompt is [abis]
s                   # ...sacrifice
@dump:offer            # so the check can prove WHICH corpse [w] is
w                   # [w] dwarf corpse (on floor)

@dump:sacrifice
@quit
